{"family": "yolox", "task": "detection", "name": "YOLOX (tiny / S / M / L / X)", "plain": "Megvii's YOLOX (tiny, s, m, l, x on COCO): anchor-free one-stage box detector, a CSPDarknet CNN with a decoupled head and NMS. Apache-2.0 code and weights.", "summary": "YOLOX (Ge et al. 2021, Megvii): anchor-free one-stage detector, all convolutions: a CSPDarknet backbone, a PAFPN neck and a decoupled head that predicts, per cell of the stride 8 / 16 / 32 maps, a box (centre and size), an objectness and a score per class; a cell's score is objectness x its best class; class-wise NMS. COCO checkpoints (80 classes) from the authors. The image is fitted into 640 x 640 (tiny: 416 x 416); vendored from the reference (no yolox dependency). The portable `module()` is the whole network (decoded boxes, scores and labels per cell, before NMS).", "tier": "experimental", "upstream": "https://github.com/Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX", "upstream_commit": "6ddff4824372906469a7fae2dc3206c7aa4bbaee", "original_is": null, "papers": [{"title": "YOLOX: Exceeding YOLO Series in 2021", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.08430", "date": "2021-07-18", "venue": "arXiv", "variants": []}], "official": [], "modes": ["portable", "kernels"], "portable_dtype": "float16", "kernels_dtype": "float16", "kernel_libs": ["cudnn_hacc", "fvm_conv", "fvm_extra", "fvm_mb", "fvm_r3"], "mps_kernel_libs": [], "mps_dtypes": ["float32", "float16"], "no_kernels_reason": "", "no_original_reason": "", "options": [{"name": "score_threshold", "default": 0.05, "bounds": "0.0 to 1.0", "effect": "output"}, {"name": "max_detections", "default": 100, "bounds": ">= 1", "effect": "output"}, {"name": "cuda_graphs", "default": true, "bounds": "", "effect": "speed"}], "outputs": [{"name": "boxes", "extra": false}, {"name": "scores", "extra": false}, {"name": "labels", "extra": false}], "output_info": {"label_set": "coco-80"}, "licence_files": ["LICENSE"], "licence_notes": [], "limitations": ["The image is resized like OpenCV 4's 8-bit INTER_LINEAR (what the reference calls); OpenCV 5 resizes differently by up to two grey levels, so a reference run on OpenCV 5 differs slightly.", "Boxes are not clamped to the image, as upstream: at the right or bottom border they can reach a few pixels into the padding.", "One label per box (the cell's best class), as upstream: a cell does not report a second class.", "Kernels keep CUDA graphs: their private pool and static outputs stay reserved, so peak reserved is ~60 MiB above portable at 640 x 480 and ~100 MiB at 1920 x 1080 (116 vs 56, 196 vs 94 MiB; peak allocated is not); `cuda_graphs=false` or `release_graphs()` frees it."], "task_io": "Input: one RGB image. Output: boxes, class labels, scores and instance masks.", "install": {"extras": ["torchvision"], "noncommercial_weights": []}, "variants": [{"id": "yolox-tiny", "released": "0.3.0", "added_in": "0.2.0", "ref": "yolox-tiny@1", "name": "yolox-tiny", "setting": "", "default_tag": false, "params": {"size": 416, "depth": 0.33, "width": 0.375}, "licence": {"code": "Apache-2.0", "code_class": "permissive", "weights": "Apache-2.0", "weights_assumed": false, "evidence": "https://github.com/Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX/blob/6ddff4824372906469a7fae2dc3206c7aa4bbaee/LICENSE (Apache-2.0); https://github.com/Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX/releases/tag/0.1.1rc0 (the weights)", "training_data": [{"id": "coco", "name": "COCO 2017 (train, instance annotations)", "licence": "CC-BY-4.0", "commercial": "unclear", "url": "https://cocodataset.org/#termsofuse"}], "training_note": "COCO 2017 train, 300 epochs from scratch (no ImageNet pretraining; Ge et al. 2021, section 2.1)", "commercial": "yes", "reasons": [], "notes": ["data: coco (unclear)"]}, "weights": [{"name": "yolox_tiny.pth", "sha256": "9de513de589ac98bb92d3bca53b5af7b9acfa9b0bacb831f7999d0f7afaee8f0", "size": 40755013, "url": "https://github.com/Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX/releases/download/0.1.1rc0/yolox_tiny.pth", "host": "GitHub", "member": null, "archive_size": null, "mir